  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Next round of showers, with a few afternoon rumbles \nof thunder possible Saturday into Saturday night\n\nAfter a brief period of dry time this afternoon and tonight due to a \npassing bubble of high pressure into the Mid-Atlantic, a southern \nstream shortwave and upper level jet will support a baroclinic wave \nto develop and track from the Ohio Valley into Pennsylvania \novernight. Meanwhile along the northern edge of the baroclinic wave \nincrease frontogensis combined with thermal packing will support \nanother period of rain to the Southern Tier overnight through \nSaturday morning. This patch of rain will move into the Finger Lakes \nand Central NY for a few hours Saturday morning, with dry weather \nprevailing to the north and west.\n\nThe next cold front will slide east across the Great Lakes Saturday \nafternoon, supporting the next chance for scattered showers. Due to \nthe arrival of the cold front being during peak diurnal heating, \nample instability, shear, moisture, and lift will support afternoon \nthunderstorms, where an isolated storm may become severe with the \nmain threats being winds and hail.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Periods of unsettled and cool conditions to \npersist well into next week. \n\nIn the wake of a weak surface ridge passing across the Great Lakes \nfor Mother's Day throughout the start of the new work week, \nadditional shortwave trough passages will round the base of the \nlongwave trough overhead, supporting continued chances for wet and \ncool conditions Wednesday through the end of the week.",
